<title>USA: Tele-Communications Intl president resigns.</title>
<headline>Tele-Communications Intl president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD, Colo. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications International Inc said on Friday that President and Chief Operating Officer Adam Singer has resigned to become chairman of its UK programming subsidiary.</p>
<p>Singer is to assume the full-time chairmanship of Flextech Plc, the company said.</p>
<p>Singer's responsibilities are to be carried out jointly by Chief Executive Fred Vierra and the company's executive vice presidents, Miranda Curtis and Graham Hollis, it said.</p>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc is the parent company of Tele-Communications International Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
